{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfyjqYcbGb8pfrvkLUuQX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No. You'd be tuning a guess about something your generator already knows. Every figure's position and size are numbers your code chose. A pixel detector tries to work backward from the rendered PNG to recover those numbers, and it picks up noise from anti-aliasing, white figure backgrounds against white slides, JPEG artifacts and figures that legitimately touch the edge. Three detectors in a row giving noisy results is a sign the approach is wrong, not that the thresholds are. If you tune hard enough to silence the noise, you'll probably start missing real clipping too.\n\n**Check the geometry where it's created.** Have the generator record each figure's box and assert it fits inside the slide, using the same numbers it used to place the figure:\n\n```python\ndef check_bounds(slide_idx, name, x, y, w, h, slide_w, slide_h, margin=0):\n    problems = []\n    if x < margin:                    problems.append(f\"left edge {x} < {margin}\")\n    if y < margin:                    problems.append(f\"top edge {y} < {margin}\")\n    if x + w > slide_w - margin:      problems.append(f\"right overflow by {x + w - (slide_w - margin)}\")\n    if y + h > slide_h - margin:      problems.append(f\"bottom overflow by {y + h - (slide_h - margin)}\")\n    if problems:\n        raise ValueError(f\"slide {slide_idx}, {name}: \" + \"; \".join(problems))\n```\n\nCall it right where each figure is placed, so the build fails at the slide and figure that caused the problem. This check is exact, gives the same answer every run, and has no thresholds to tune. You can also add a pairwise overlap check between figures on the same slide.\n\n**Geometry won't catch everything. Cover these separately:**\n- **Rotation and group transforms.** Check the box after rotation or the group's scaling, not the raw width and height.\n- **Cropping inside the image.** A box can sit fully on the slide while the picture inside it is cut off, for example by crop settings or by fitting an image into a box with a different aspect ratio. Assert that the crop values are zero, or that the aspect ratios match.\n- **Text overflowing its box.** Box coordinates don't tell you whether the text fits. Measure the text with the actual font (e.g. PIL `ImageFont.getbbox`), or check that auto-fit or shrink-on-overflow is set the way you expect.\n- **Positions inherited from layouts or placeholders.** If a figure takes its position from a template instead of your code, read back the final position from the saved file rather than trusting what you passed in.\n- **Differences between renderers.** LibreOffice and PowerPoint can lay text out differently. Geometry is reliable for images and shapes, less so for text.\n\n**Keep the PNGs for people to look at.** A contact sheet of thumbnails lets you scan a whole deck in seconds for problems no check will catch, like a figure that's technically in bounds but looks wrong. If you want to keep one automated pixel check, keep it simple: look for content in a few-pixel band along the slide edges and treat it as a warning, not a pass/fail result.\n\nIf you tell me which library you use (python-pptx, reportlab, matplotlib, something else), I can show you where to put the hook and how to read the final positions back from the saved file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12150,"cache_read_input_tokens":25083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12150},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff01f16c-7b3f-5ea5-8051-7a95ac7cd1d1","uuid":"4498eb38-094d-41f3-b6bd-2be663fff41d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T06:10:42.959Z","request